WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.322 --> 00:00:04.555
- Good morning Believe Nation.

00:00:04.555 --> 00:00:05.744
Today we're going to talk about

00:00:05.744 --> 00:00:08.556
how you can be more persuasive.

00:00:08.556 --> 00:00:10.180
Rule number two is my personal favorite

00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:11.670
and I'm curious to figure out which one

00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:12.967
you guys like the best,

00:00:12.967 --> 00:00:14.566
and as always guys, as you're listening,

00:00:14.566 --> 00:00:15.582
if you hear something

00:00:15.582 --> 00:00:16.796
that really, really resonates with you,

00:00:16.796 --> 00:00:18.342
please leave it in the comments below,

00:00:18.342 --> 00:00:19.175
and put quotes around it

00:00:19.175 --> 00:00:20.744
so other people can be inspired

00:00:20.744 --> 00:00:22.585
and also as you write things down,

00:00:22.585 --> 00:00:27.110
you're much more likely to
keep it in here as well.

00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:27.943
Enjoy.

00:00:30.344 --> 00:00:32.927
(bright music)

00:00:46.171 --> 00:00:48.269
- What I want you to get

00:00:48.269 --> 00:00:50.572
is the single most
important skill in life,

00:00:50.572 --> 00:00:51.949
we hate the word selling,

00:00:51.949 --> 00:00:54.063
so I'll give you a word that it really is,

00:00:54.063 --> 00:00:55.960
that doesn't have the
negative connotation.

00:00:55.960 --> 00:00:59.127
It's the word that all leaders have.

00:00:59.127 --> 00:01:00.892
What would that word be?

00:01:00.892 --> 00:01:01.725
Influence.

00:01:03.503 --> 00:01:05.490
What changes companies

00:01:05.490 --> 00:01:07.054
is leaders.

00:01:07.054 --> 00:01:09.421
The only way to change
a company is leadership.

00:01:09.421 --> 00:01:11.008
If I want to change a company that I own,

00:01:11.008 --> 00:01:12.260
and I want to make a
shift in that company,

00:01:12.260 --> 00:01:14.970
the number one thing I want
to do is shifting leadership.

00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:16.957
That might be taking
leaders to a different level

00:01:16.957 --> 00:01:17.944
that might be bringing new leaders in,

00:01:17.944 --> 00:01:19.582
that might be new leaders with new voices,

00:01:19.582 --> 00:01:21.402
with new perspectives,

00:01:21.402 --> 00:01:23.390
with new skills sets, new directions.

00:01:23.390 --> 00:01:25.630
But we need to take
things to another level.

00:01:25.630 --> 00:01:26.953
Leaders solve problems

00:01:26.953 --> 00:01:29.105
and leaders maximize resources.

00:01:29.105 --> 00:01:30.254
If you're going to solve problems,

00:01:30.254 --> 00:01:31.274
you can't do it yourself

00:01:31.274 --> 00:01:33.700
or it would have already been solved.

00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:35.364
You have to get others
to help you to do it.

00:01:35.364 --> 00:01:37.265
That requires influence.

00:01:37.265 --> 00:01:38.604
True?

00:01:38.604 --> 00:01:40.518
If you're going to get
people to maximize resources

00:01:40.518 --> 00:01:42.518
that requires influence.

00:01:43.718 --> 00:01:45.091
If you're going to get
people to partner with you,

00:01:45.091 --> 00:01:47.388
provide you resources, capital,

00:01:47.388 --> 00:01:49.222
suppliers, anything,

00:01:49.222 --> 00:01:51.222
that requires influence.

00:01:52.588 --> 00:01:54.038
If you're going to have
an impact on your kids

00:01:54.038 --> 00:01:56.952
or your community or the world,

00:01:56.952 --> 00:01:57.962
that requires influence.

00:01:57.962 --> 00:01:59.909
There is no more important skill

00:01:59.909 --> 00:02:02.356
of leadership than influence.

00:02:02.356 --> 00:02:05.602
And yet most of us think
of it like selling.

00:02:05.602 --> 00:02:07.963
And as a result we don't master influence.

00:02:07.963 --> 00:02:09.550
'Cause I know if you can't influence,

00:02:09.550 --> 00:02:10.800
you can't lead.

00:02:11.653 --> 00:02:13.312
But if you can influence powerfully,

00:02:13.312 --> 00:02:15.842
intelligently, with integrity,

00:02:15.842 --> 00:02:17.667
there is no limit to
whatever you can envision

00:02:17.667 --> 00:02:19.129
and what you can make real.

00:02:19.129 --> 00:02:21.771
And if you're influence becomes
not just use the influence

00:02:21.771 --> 00:02:23.690
but you're able to
influence systems, people,

00:02:23.690 --> 00:02:25.107
company, culture,

00:02:26.455 --> 00:02:29.724
if you can turn other
people into influencers,

00:02:29.724 --> 00:02:33.891
now whatever you vision about
can be made into reality.

00:02:36.687 --> 00:02:38.490
- So let me give you a hypothetical

00:02:38.490 --> 00:02:39.879
suppose that you're a parent

00:02:39.879 --> 00:02:41.516
and you have a daughter,

00:02:41.516 --> 00:02:43.101
say a teenage daughter

00:02:43.101 --> 00:02:45.110
who's room is an absolute mess.

00:02:45.110 --> 00:02:47.731
It just looks like a
bomb went off in there

00:02:47.731 --> 00:02:49.961
and you want your daughter
to clean her room.

00:02:49.961 --> 00:02:51.002
You're trying to sell her on the idea

00:02:51.002 --> 00:02:52.123
of cleaning her room.

00:02:52.123 --> 00:02:53.134
What do you do?

00:02:53.134 --> 00:02:55.122
Well, you could try to bribe her,

00:02:55.122 --> 00:02:56.527
and that might work in the short term.

00:02:56.527 --> 00:02:58.412
You could try to threaten her,

00:02:58.412 --> 00:02:59.913
that might work in the short term.

00:02:59.913 --> 00:03:01.488
You can try to exhort her,

00:03:01.488 --> 00:03:02.700
you can try to, you know,

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:05.060
tell her about the meaning of clean rooms,

00:03:05.060 --> 00:03:07.427
but there's actually a technique

00:03:07.427 --> 00:03:10.688
from actually the counseling literature,

00:03:10.688 --> 00:03:12.340
really crystallized by a fellow named

00:03:12.340 --> 00:03:15.033
Mike Pantalon of Yale University

00:03:15.033 --> 00:03:16.799
called Motivational Interviewing,

00:03:16.799 --> 00:03:19.333
and what you can do, more effectively

00:03:19.333 --> 00:03:21.465
is ask two irrational questions.

00:03:21.465 --> 00:03:24.492
So, let's say you have
a daughter named Maria

00:03:24.492 --> 00:03:26.524
and Maria has a messy room

00:03:26.524 --> 00:03:28.161
and you want Maria to clean her room.

00:03:28.161 --> 00:03:30.102
The two questions you
could ask Maria are this,

00:03:30.102 --> 00:03:32.685
Maria, on a scale of one to 10,

00:03:34.118 --> 00:03:36.854
one meaning I'm not ready at all,

00:03:36.854 --> 00:03:39.173
10 meaning I'm ready to do it right now,

00:03:39.173 --> 00:03:43.053
ow ready are you Maria,
to clean your room?

00:03:43.053 --> 00:03:45.424
Now, Maria's room is a pigsty,

00:03:45.424 --> 00:03:48.688
so she's not going to
give you a 10 or a nine,

00:03:48.688 --> 00:03:49.749
or even a five.

00:03:49.749 --> 00:03:51.242
Maybe she'll give you a two, okay.

00:03:51.242 --> 00:03:53.706
So she says, "Dad, I'm a two."

00:03:53.706 --> 00:03:56.134
Well here's where the
second question comes in

00:03:56.134 --> 00:03:58.781
and it's a really interesting
counter intuitive question.

00:03:58.781 --> 00:04:02.224
You say to Maria, "Okay
Maria, you're a two.

00:04:02.224 --> 00:04:05.746
Why don't you pick a lower number?"

00:04:05.746 --> 00:04:07.567
Now our instincts as parents is to say,

00:04:07.567 --> 00:04:08.567
as a parent of three kids,

00:04:08.567 --> 00:04:10.579
I have this instinct very strongly.

00:04:10.579 --> 00:04:11.820
If my kid were to say to me, "I'm a two,"

00:04:11.820 --> 00:04:13.431
I would say, "What, why are you a two,

00:04:13.431 --> 00:04:14.916
you should be a nine."

00:04:14.916 --> 00:04:18.282
But you say, "Why don't you
pick a lower number, Maria?"

00:04:18.282 --> 00:04:19.115
So here's what happens,

00:04:19.115 --> 00:04:23.077
Maria has to explain why
she isn't a one, okay?

00:04:23.077 --> 00:04:25.496
And so she says, "Well, you know,

00:04:25.496 --> 00:04:29.694
I am 15 and I probably
should get my act together,

00:04:29.694 --> 00:04:31.249
you know if I had my room cleaner,

00:04:31.249 --> 00:04:32.668
I'd be able to get to school on time,

00:04:32.668 --> 00:04:35.802
faster and maybe see my
friends a little bit more.

00:04:35.802 --> 00:04:38.384
You know you and mom never
know where anything is anyway,

00:04:38.384 --> 00:04:39.498
so I'm kind of wasting my time

00:04:39.498 --> 00:04:41.256
asking you to help me."

00:04:41.256 --> 00:04:43.557
What happens, with that second question,

00:04:43.557 --> 00:04:45.149
why did you pick a lower number,

00:04:45.149 --> 00:04:48.030
Maria begins articulating her own reasons

00:04:48.030 --> 00:04:49.105
for doing something.

00:04:49.105 --> 00:04:52.860
And this is really axiomatic
in sales and persuasion.

00:04:52.860 --> 00:04:56.039
When people have their own
reasons for doing something,

00:04:56.039 --> 00:04:58.654
not yours, their own
reasons for doing something,

00:04:58.654 --> 00:05:00.707
they believe those reasons more deeply

00:05:00.707 --> 00:05:04.124
and adhere to the behavior more strongly.

00:05:09.794 --> 00:05:11.703
Now suppose Maria says,

00:05:11.703 --> 00:05:15.813
"Dad, on a scale on one to 10, I'm a one."

00:05:15.813 --> 00:05:17.226
That makes things a
little more complicated.

00:05:17.226 --> 00:05:18.938
But it's actually really, really important

00:05:18.938 --> 00:05:20.099
to understand this.

00:05:20.099 --> 00:05:21.405
If you say to Maria,

00:05:21.405 --> 00:05:23.706
if Maria says, "Dad, I'm a one."

00:05:23.706 --> 00:05:25.181
Here's what you say to Maria.

00:05:25.181 --> 00:05:28.466
"Maria, what can we do to make you a two?"

00:05:28.466 --> 00:05:30.495
And what often that does is this,

00:05:30.495 --> 00:05:32.994
Maria will say, "Well maybe
if you and mom help me

00:05:32.994 --> 00:05:35.502
for 15 minutes to get this started.

00:05:35.502 --> 00:05:38.448
Maybe if you, maybe not set the table

00:05:38.448 --> 00:05:39.822
and take out the trash tonight,

00:05:39.822 --> 00:05:41.106
that would free up some time for me."

00:05:41.106 --> 00:05:43.898
'Cause usually when people are a one,

00:05:43.898 --> 00:05:46.889
it's often not because
they're purely obstinate,

00:05:46.889 --> 00:05:49.378
it's because there is some
kind of environmental obstacle

00:05:49.378 --> 00:05:51.176
in front of them

00:05:51.176 --> 00:05:53.440
and if someone says they're a one,

00:05:53.440 --> 00:05:55.451
find out what that obstacle is,

00:05:55.451 --> 00:05:56.652
try to make them a two,

00:05:56.652 --> 00:05:58.255
and that might give
you some more momentum.

00:05:58.255 --> 00:05:59.570
The example I just gave

00:05:59.570 --> 00:06:01.134
had to do with parenting,

00:06:01.134 --> 00:06:03.049
but you can use this more universally.

00:06:03.049 --> 00:06:04.176
Now you can't whip it out

00:06:04.176 --> 00:06:06.850
at every single persuasive encounter.

00:06:06.850 --> 00:06:09.588
But you can use it to persuade your boss,

00:06:09.588 --> 00:06:14.468
you can use it, maybe, to
persuade a reluctant prospect

00:06:14.468 --> 00:06:16.783
in an actual sales encounter.

00:06:16.783 --> 00:06:20.466
You can use it with
someone, your neighbor,

00:06:20.466 --> 00:06:22.623
who is resisting moving his garbage cans,

00:06:22.623 --> 00:06:23.844
or something like that.

00:06:23.844 --> 00:06:24.984
The key here, and again,

00:06:24.984 --> 00:06:26.653
you got to go back to
first principles here.

00:06:26.653 --> 00:06:30.338
The key here is that we tend
to think that persuasion

00:06:30.338 --> 00:06:35.001
or motivation is something
that one person does to another

00:06:35.001 --> 00:06:37.495
and what the social science
tells us very clearly,

00:06:37.495 --> 00:06:39.822
is that it's really
something that people do

00:06:39.822 --> 00:06:41.049
for themselves,

00:06:41.049 --> 00:06:43.721
and your job as a
persuader, as a motivator,

00:06:43.721 --> 00:06:45.613
is to reset the context

00:06:45.613 --> 00:06:48.334
and surface people's own
reasons for doing something

00:06:48.334 --> 00:06:50.999
because it works a lot better.

00:06:50.999 --> 00:06:53.904
- Every phone call you make is recorded.

00:06:53.904 --> 00:06:55.041
There's no single phone call

00:06:55.041 --> 00:06:56.470
that goes in and out in North America

00:06:56.470 --> 00:06:57.495
that they don't have a recording of

00:06:57.495 --> 00:06:59.845
and they can search by word, by tone,

00:06:59.845 --> 00:07:03.094
by tempo, they can even
recognize voices now.

00:07:03.094 --> 00:07:05.469
There's no thinking of
such thing as privacy.

00:07:05.469 --> 00:07:06.706
Everything you've ever put on the Internet

00:07:06.706 --> 00:07:08.381
is there forever, and people know it,

00:07:08.381 --> 00:07:10.192
they can search it.

00:07:10.192 --> 00:07:12.844
The way you write is searchable now.

00:07:12.844 --> 00:07:13.786
You cannot sign your email,

00:07:13.786 --> 00:07:15.742
you can put it on somebody else's email

00:07:15.742 --> 00:07:17.057
and the structure of your language

00:07:17.057 --> 00:07:19.176
and the way you influence things

00:07:19.176 --> 00:07:21.081
can be studied at this level.

00:07:21.081 --> 00:07:22.674
So, the good news about that is

00:07:22.674 --> 00:07:26.841
manipulation as an ongoing
tool for success is over,

00:07:28.046 --> 00:07:30.961
but, adding value, will
never go out of style.

00:07:30.961 --> 00:07:32.625
Truth will never go out of style.

00:07:32.625 --> 00:07:35.494
So influencing with
integrity is the secret.

00:07:35.494 --> 00:07:37.087
But what really influences people?

00:07:37.087 --> 00:07:38.067
Do facts and figures,

00:07:38.067 --> 00:07:39.240
if we're giving you facts and figures

00:07:39.240 --> 00:07:40.101
out of a core story,

00:07:40.101 --> 00:07:42.559
is that going to influence people?

00:07:42.559 --> 00:07:43.392
No.

00:07:44.349 --> 00:07:47.484
It's the weaving of that
story together in a way

00:07:47.484 --> 00:07:49.384
that produces what shifts people.

00:07:49.384 --> 00:07:51.046
And that's human emotion.

00:07:51.046 --> 00:07:54.634
Ultimately, the big game here is emotion.

00:07:54.634 --> 00:07:55.680
You have to influence emotion.

00:07:55.680 --> 00:07:57.236
You have to influence the
emotion of your people.

00:07:57.236 --> 00:07:59.100
If you're going to maximize resources,

00:07:59.100 --> 00:08:01.420
and if we all agree, as we
talked about the other day,

00:08:01.420 --> 00:08:03.075
it's not a lack of resources,

00:08:03.075 --> 00:08:05.154
it's a lack of, what?

00:08:05.154 --> 00:08:06.061
Resourcefulness.

00:08:06.061 --> 00:08:07.781
If you're creative enough,
if you're playful enough,

00:08:07.781 --> 00:08:09.139
if you're determined enough,

00:08:09.139 --> 00:08:11.399
if you're focused enough,

00:08:11.399 --> 00:08:12.232
you can find a way.

00:08:12.232 --> 00:08:13.104
If you're giving enough,

00:08:13.104 --> 00:08:15.062
if you're generous enough,
if you're honest enough,

00:08:15.062 --> 00:08:16.358
if you're courageous enough,

00:08:16.358 --> 00:08:17.879
you will get people to help you,

00:08:17.879 --> 00:08:18.847
you will find the way,

00:08:18.847 --> 00:08:20.462
you will make that thing happen.

00:08:20.462 --> 00:08:22.047
You'll access the resource.

00:08:22.047 --> 00:08:23.509
You'll get someone to
coach you, teach you,

00:08:23.509 --> 00:08:25.627
loan it to you, let you try it, drive it,

00:08:25.627 --> 00:08:26.794
experience it.

00:08:28.737 --> 00:08:29.830
So it's the ability to influence emotion,

00:08:29.830 --> 00:08:33.381
because that's what affects our intellect.

00:08:33.381 --> 00:08:34.214
That's the bottom line.

00:08:34.214 --> 00:08:36.466
A core story is only there

00:08:36.466 --> 00:08:38.202
to give you a set of
facts to educate someone,

00:08:38.202 --> 00:08:41.262
that will make them emotional
enough to make a decision.

00:08:41.262 --> 00:08:42.965
And what they do is they go
through a series of things

00:08:42.965 --> 00:08:44.352
that you have emotions about.

00:08:44.352 --> 00:08:45.870
They may say them in a non emotional way

00:08:45.870 --> 00:08:47.472
but the only reason the work is 'cause

00:08:47.472 --> 00:08:50.465
you know they're going to
open a person's emotion.

00:08:50.465 --> 00:08:51.861
How many agree with me on this, say I.

00:08:51.861 --> 00:08:52.697
- [Audience] I.

00:08:52.697 --> 00:08:56.208
- So as leaders, we can never forget,

00:08:56.208 --> 00:08:59.706
that humans are emotional
creatures including ourselves.

00:08:59.706 --> 00:09:02.124
And to influence other people,

00:09:02.124 --> 00:09:04.225
we have to know what
already influences them.

00:09:04.225 --> 00:09:07.334
And we can't ever forget
what truly influences them.

00:09:07.334 --> 00:09:09.656
It's going to come down to our
ability to connect with them

00:09:09.656 --> 00:09:11.301
at a deep, emotional level,

00:09:11.301 --> 00:09:13.084
or get others to do the same.

00:09:13.084 --> 00:09:14.952
- Men and women with charisma

00:09:14.952 --> 00:09:17.005
and personal magnetism,

00:09:17.005 --> 00:09:20.378
almost invariably have a
clear vision of who they are

00:09:20.378 --> 00:09:22.406
and where they're going,

00:09:22.406 --> 00:09:24.505
and what they're trying to achieve.

00:09:24.505 --> 00:09:26.769
And you can develop this as well.

00:09:26.769 --> 00:09:29.127
Leaders in sales and management

00:09:29.127 --> 00:09:31.798
have a vision of what
they're trying to create

00:09:31.798 --> 00:09:33.716
and why they're doing what they're doing.

00:09:33.716 --> 00:09:36.675
They're focused on
accomplishing some great purpose

00:09:36.675 --> 00:09:38.182
with their lives and their work.

00:09:38.182 --> 00:09:40.528
They're decisive about
every aspect of their lives.

00:09:40.528 --> 00:09:43.932
They know exactly what they want

00:09:43.932 --> 00:09:45.931
and what they have to do to get it.

00:09:45.931 --> 00:09:49.723
They plan their work and
then they work their plan.

00:09:49.723 --> 00:09:51.874
You can increase your charisma

00:09:51.874 --> 00:09:54.644
and the magnetism of your personality

00:09:54.644 --> 00:09:57.507
by setting clear goals for yourself.

00:09:57.507 --> 00:09:59.964
Making plans to achieve them

00:09:59.964 --> 00:10:02.599
and then working on your
plans with discipline

00:10:02.599 --> 00:10:05.571
and determination every day.

00:10:05.571 --> 00:10:07.801
The whole world seems to move aside

00:10:07.801 --> 00:10:11.491
for the person who knows
exactly where he's going.

00:10:11.491 --> 00:10:15.302
In fact, the clearer you are
about your purposes and goals,

00:10:15.302 --> 00:10:18.138
the more likely people
will be to attribute

00:10:18.138 --> 00:10:20.803
other positive qualities to you.

00:10:20.803 --> 00:10:22.223
When you're clear about your goals,

00:10:22.223 --> 00:10:24.554
people will see you or perceive you

00:10:24.554 --> 00:10:28.524
as being a better and more
admirable human being.

00:10:28.524 --> 00:10:30.101
And when you have clear goals,

00:10:30.101 --> 00:10:32.022
you begin attracting to yourself

00:10:32.022 --> 00:10:34.770
the people and opportunities necessary

00:10:34.770 --> 00:10:37.893
to make those goals a reality.

00:10:37.893 --> 00:10:40.074
- In Robert Cialdini's book, Influence,

00:10:40.074 --> 00:10:43.616
he says, "A well-known
principle of human behavior

00:10:43.616 --> 00:10:46.185
says that when we ask
someone to do us a favor,

00:10:46.185 --> 00:10:49.735
we will be more successful
if we provide a reason."

00:10:49.735 --> 00:10:51.094
Here's an example from that book,

00:10:51.094 --> 00:10:52.080
listen to this,

00:10:52.080 --> 00:10:54.356
A woman was standing in
line for a copy machine

00:10:54.356 --> 00:10:57.562
and she said, "Excuse
me, I have five pages,

00:10:57.562 --> 00:11:00.110
may I go ahead of you and make my copies?"

00:11:00.110 --> 00:11:01.891
60% of people said yes.

00:11:01.891 --> 00:11:03.344
Now listen to this.

00:11:03.344 --> 00:11:06.118
She tried asking a slightly different way.

00:11:06.118 --> 00:11:07.951
She gave a reason why.

00:11:08.961 --> 00:11:11.035
This time she said, "Excuse me,

00:11:11.035 --> 00:11:13.780
I have five pages, may
I use the copy machine

00:11:13.780 --> 00:11:16.277
because I'm in a rush?"

00:11:16.277 --> 00:11:19.666
And this time, 94% of the people said yes,

00:11:19.666 --> 00:11:21.572
that's one and a half times as many.

00:11:21.572 --> 00:11:23.417
That is a lot of persuasion.

00:11:23.417 --> 00:11:24.583
Now there's more to that study

00:11:24.583 --> 00:11:26.529
and you can check it
out in Cialdini's book.

00:11:26.529 --> 00:11:28.248
But the point here is

00:11:28.248 --> 00:11:30.188
that when you give people a reason why

00:11:30.188 --> 00:11:31.654
you're asking for something,

00:11:31.654 --> 00:11:33.901
They're more inclined to give it to you.

00:11:33.901 --> 00:11:35.821
- How do I add more value

00:11:35.821 --> 00:11:37.188
so that I can get paid more?

00:11:37.188 --> 00:11:38.777
So that I can have more influence.

00:11:38.777 --> 00:11:41.701
So that I can make more of
a difference where I'm at.

00:11:41.701 --> 00:11:43.653
You always hear it all the time, right?

00:11:43.653 --> 00:11:44.976
Add more value.

00:11:44.976 --> 00:11:46.450
Well how?

00:11:46.450 --> 00:11:47.983
How do you add more value

00:11:47.983 --> 00:11:50.202
so you can get paid more
and have more influence?

00:11:50.202 --> 00:11:53.304
Part of adding value is
helping people reconnect

00:11:53.304 --> 00:11:55.913
with some emotional side of their lives.

00:11:55.913 --> 00:11:58.167
I know that sounds so simple in some ways

00:11:58.167 --> 00:12:00.093
but also philosophical.

00:12:00.093 --> 00:12:03.535
That a lot of what we
experience today in this world

00:12:03.535 --> 00:12:07.316
is just so cheap and so commoditized,

00:12:07.316 --> 00:12:09.234
and so technically driven

00:12:09.234 --> 00:12:12.690
that it's our job, if we
want to add a lot of value,

00:12:12.690 --> 00:12:15.114
to bring back in humanity.

00:12:15.114 --> 00:12:16.892
To bring back in the emotion,

00:12:16.892 --> 00:12:19.464
to bring back in the color, the flare,

00:12:19.464 --> 00:12:21.509
the joy, the vibrancy,

00:12:21.509 --> 00:12:24.402
the real hues of human emotion

00:12:24.402 --> 00:12:26.546
that are often missing from everything.

00:12:26.546 --> 00:12:28.698
If you bring that back in to everything

00:12:28.698 --> 00:12:29.688
that you're contributing,

00:12:29.688 --> 00:12:31.109
you'll go to a level of adding value

00:12:31.109 --> 00:12:32.683
that most people will never understand.

00:12:32.683 --> 00:12:33.988
And people won't just follow you because

00:12:33.988 --> 00:12:37.498
you're the person who
asks the best questions,

00:12:37.498 --> 00:12:38.812
people won't just follow you because

00:12:38.812 --> 00:12:40.501
you're the person who
knows the most people.

00:12:40.501 --> 00:12:43.003
People will follow you
because you're an inspirer

00:12:43.003 --> 00:12:44.118
and you're a leader.

00:12:44.118 --> 00:12:45.472
Because they can see that within you

00:12:45.472 --> 00:12:47.583
you have true energy, true engagement,

00:12:47.583 --> 00:12:49.083
true human emotion

00:12:50.099 --> 00:12:51.655
with everything that you're contributing

00:12:51.655 --> 00:12:53.765
and because of that, they
know that you're somebody

00:12:53.765 --> 00:12:55.819
they want to follow.

00:12:55.819 --> 00:12:56.707
- So my take on this,

00:12:56.707 --> 00:12:58.301
is if you want to be more persuasive,

00:12:58.301 --> 00:12:59.686
then you need to care more.

00:12:59.686 --> 00:13:00.750
You need to care more,

00:13:00.750 --> 00:13:02.730
and the care comes from two sides.

00:13:02.730 --> 00:13:04.945
First it's you caring
more about it yourself,

00:13:04.945 --> 00:13:06.583
having more passion in it.

00:13:06.583 --> 00:13:07.721
When you have passion,

00:13:07.721 --> 00:13:08.765
when you're excited about something,

00:13:08.765 --> 00:13:10.161
people want to join you,

00:13:10.161 --> 00:13:11.430
people want to be around people

00:13:11.430 --> 00:13:13.257
who are passionate about something.

00:13:13.257 --> 00:13:15.514
You can gear somebody towards something

00:13:15.514 --> 00:13:17.537
because you have the passion for it.

00:13:17.537 --> 00:13:19.240
Sam Walton from Walmart used to say

00:13:19.240 --> 00:13:20.792
that passion is so important

00:13:20.792 --> 00:13:22.931
and that people will
catch it like a fever.

00:13:22.931 --> 00:13:25.182
If you have a fever, other
people will catch it.

00:13:25.182 --> 00:13:27.212
If you have a cold, other
people will catch it.

00:13:27.212 --> 00:13:29.824
If you have a passion,
other people will catch it.

00:13:29.824 --> 00:13:31.685
So if you want to be more persuasive,

00:13:31.685 --> 00:13:33.241
when you're saying these words

00:13:33.241 --> 00:13:34.616
that it's really going to help somebody,

00:13:34.616 --> 00:13:35.957
whatever it is, your product or service

00:13:35.957 --> 00:13:36.830
you're trying to promote,

00:13:36.830 --> 00:13:37.951
your book, your YouTube channel,

00:13:37.951 --> 00:13:40.349
whatever it is, if you are excited,

00:13:40.349 --> 00:13:41.789
and it comes through in every word

00:13:41.789 --> 00:13:43.002
that comes out of your mouth,

00:13:43.002 --> 00:13:44.515
it's going to be much more persuasive

00:13:44.515 --> 00:13:45.661
to the people listening,

00:13:45.661 --> 00:13:47.553
than if you're really boring,

00:13:47.553 --> 00:13:49.992
and saying, "Yeah, I
have a YouTube channel,

00:13:49.992 --> 00:13:51.056
you should check it out.

00:13:51.056 --> 00:13:52.451
There's some good stuff on there."

00:13:52.451 --> 00:13:53.812
It's just a different vibe.

00:13:53.812 --> 00:13:55.124
You don't want to go check that thing out.

00:13:55.124 --> 00:13:56.216
When somebodies excited,

00:13:56.216 --> 00:13:57.413
like I want to piece of that.

00:13:57.413 --> 00:13:59.256
I want more excitement
and passion in my life

00:13:59.256 --> 00:14:00.460
and so I'm going to go check it out.

00:14:00.460 --> 00:14:02.371
So that happens when you care more.

00:14:02.371 --> 00:14:04.331
So care more and tie in to the why,

00:14:04.331 --> 00:14:06.642
and remember before going
in to every conversation,

00:14:06.642 --> 00:14:08.778
why this is so important.

00:14:08.778 --> 00:14:10.496
To you and to them.

00:14:10.496 --> 00:14:11.436
The second part of care

00:14:11.436 --> 00:14:12.655
is caring about them.

00:14:12.655 --> 00:14:14.155
Caring about their best interests,

00:14:14.155 --> 00:14:16.628
caring about what they
want to do in their life,

00:14:16.628 --> 00:14:17.578
in their business

00:14:17.578 --> 00:14:19.504
and the result that they
are trying to achieve

00:14:19.504 --> 00:14:21.701
and how you can potentially help them.

00:14:21.701 --> 00:14:22.995
If you have a product or service

00:14:22.995 --> 00:14:25.415
that can help somebody
solve a critical problem,

00:14:25.415 --> 00:14:28.551
then it's your responsibility
to show you care to them.

00:14:28.551 --> 00:14:31.168
If they can feel that you
actually care about them,

00:14:31.168 --> 00:14:32.557
that you're not just trying to sell them

00:14:32.557 --> 00:14:34.079
your product or service,

00:14:34.079 --> 00:14:37.165
that you actually deep down
care about their success,

00:14:37.165 --> 00:14:38.999
they're going to be much
more receptive to it.

00:14:38.999 --> 00:14:41.184
You're going to be much
more persuasive to them.

00:14:41.184 --> 00:14:42.017
I think with all of this,

00:14:42.017 --> 00:14:43.508
it's not just about trying
to convince somebody

00:14:43.508 --> 00:14:45.697
to do something that they
don't really want to do,

00:14:45.697 --> 00:14:47.571
I think the ultimate persuasion comes from

00:14:47.571 --> 00:14:49.345
helping them realize
that this is something

00:14:49.345 --> 00:14:50.706
that they want to do.

00:14:50.706 --> 00:14:53.019
That your product or service
will actually help them.

00:14:53.019 --> 00:14:54.281
If you look at my YouTube videos,

00:14:54.281 --> 00:14:56.556
I don't care if your
guys watch every video,

00:14:56.556 --> 00:14:57.605
I'd actually prefer that you don't

00:14:57.605 --> 00:14:58.481
watch every video.

00:14:58.481 --> 00:14:59.622
I want you to watch the video

00:14:59.622 --> 00:15:01.791
that has the most
meaning and impact to you

00:15:01.791 --> 00:15:03.187
and then go take some kind of action.

00:15:03.187 --> 00:15:04.762
The best thing from YouTube's perspective

00:15:04.762 --> 00:15:07.466
is spend all day long on
YouTube watching my videos.

00:15:07.466 --> 00:15:08.433
I don't want that to happen.

00:15:08.433 --> 00:15:09.802
I want you to watch the videos

00:15:09.802 --> 00:15:10.926
and then go take action.

00:15:10.926 --> 00:15:13.236
Stop watching and go do
something in your life

00:15:13.236 --> 00:15:14.074
or your business.

00:15:14.074 --> 00:15:15.458
And if you need to watch these videos

00:15:15.458 --> 00:15:17.349
as a way to get more inspiration,

00:15:17.349 --> 00:15:18.357
to get more motivation,

00:15:18.357 --> 00:15:20.202
to get more strategies
and tactics and ideas

00:15:20.202 --> 00:15:22.257
to do something, that's great.

00:15:22.257 --> 00:15:23.337
Make that part of your daily routine.

00:15:23.337 --> 00:15:24.279
Amazing.

00:15:24.279 --> 00:15:26.347
And then go take some action.

00:15:26.347 --> 00:15:28.655
And hopefully you feel
that care that I have

00:15:28.655 --> 00:15:29.488
for you guys.

00:15:29.488 --> 00:15:31.630
I deeply want you to be successful.

00:15:31.630 --> 00:15:34.779
I want, more than I want you
to be on my YouTube channel,

00:15:34.779 --> 00:15:37.718
I want you to have success with your plan.

00:15:37.718 --> 00:15:39.498
I want this year to be amazing for you.

00:15:39.498 --> 00:15:41.183
I want you to get this
thing out of your head

00:15:41.183 --> 00:15:42.763
and out into the world,

00:15:42.763 --> 00:15:44.762
having a big impact,
making a lot of money,

00:15:44.762 --> 00:15:46.305
having the life that you want to live,

00:15:46.305 --> 00:15:47.348
and reaching your potential.

00:15:47.348 --> 00:15:48.577
This is what fuels me.

00:15:48.577 --> 00:15:50.785
And so when I speak like that,

00:15:50.785 --> 00:15:52.926
when I connect with people in that way,

00:15:52.926 --> 00:15:55.733
they feel the care that I have for them

00:15:55.733 --> 00:15:57.948
and that makes a huge,
huge, huge difference.

00:15:57.948 --> 00:16:01.255
So, my tip to be more
persuasive is to care.

00:16:01.255 --> 00:16:02.416
Care more for yourself,

00:16:02.416 --> 00:16:04.173
care more about the passion you have

00:16:04.173 --> 00:16:06.377
for the product or service,
the industry that you're in,

00:16:06.377 --> 00:16:08.810
and then care more about the customer.

00:16:08.810 --> 00:16:11.814
Help them achieve the objective
that they want to achieve

00:16:11.814 --> 00:16:13.957
and show them that you're
not just trying to make sale,

00:16:13.957 --> 00:16:15.630
you're trying to help
them live a better life,

00:16:15.630 --> 00:16:17.292
or have a better business.

00:16:17.292 --> 00:16:18.125
Care more.

00:16:21.110 --> 00:16:22.240
Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:16:22.240 --> 00:16:25.462
I made this video because
Sushmita Ojha asked me to.

00:16:25.462 --> 00:16:26.611
So if there's a topic
you'd like me to cover

00:16:26.611 --> 00:16:28.573
in the next edition of Believe Life,

00:16:28.573 --> 00:16:29.891
leave it down in the comments below

00:16:29.891 --> 00:16:31.025
and I'll see what I can do.

00:16:31.025 --> 00:16:31.858
I'd also love to know,

00:16:31.858 --> 00:16:32.974
what did you learn from this video?

00:16:32.974 --> 00:16:34.932
What was your favorite clip and why?

00:16:34.932 --> 00:16:37.164
How are you going to be more persuasive,

00:16:37.164 --> 00:16:39.636
or do you have a tip that
you'd like to share as well?

00:16:39.636 --> 00:16:41.467
Please leave it down
in the comments below.

00:16:41.467 --> 00:16:43.698
I'm excited to see what
you guys have to say.

00:16:43.698 --> 00:16:45.552
Finally, I want to give a
quick shout out to Fabian.

00:16:45.552 --> 00:16:47.457
Fabian, thank you so
much for the interview

00:16:47.457 --> 00:16:49.013
and for picking up a copy of my book,

00:16:49.013 --> 00:16:50.141
Your One Word.

00:16:50.141 --> 00:16:51.910
It really, really,
really means a lot to me

00:16:51.910 --> 00:16:53.330
and I hope you're enjoying the read.

00:16:53.330 --> 00:16:54.712
Thank you guys again for watching.

00:16:54.712 --> 00:16:55.970
I believe in you.

00:16:55.970 --> 00:16:57.946
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:16:57.946 --> 00:16:59.751
and whatever your one word is.

00:16:59.751 --> 00:17:02.108
Much love, have an amazing day

00:17:02.108 --> 00:17:03.941
and I'll see you soon.

00:17:09.900 --> 00:17:12.420
- If you do not know
how to persuade people,

00:17:12.420 --> 00:17:14.221
it is virtually impossible,

00:17:14.221 --> 00:17:15.542
unless you want to hit lotto.

00:17:15.542 --> 00:17:17.251
If you get lucky, you can hit lotto.

00:17:17.251 --> 00:17:18.945
Or if you remember the lucky sperm club,

00:17:18.945 --> 00:17:20.116
you inherit it from your parents.

00:17:20.116 --> 00:17:21.022
Right, well maybe yeah,

00:17:21.022 --> 00:17:23.879
you can circumvent that process.

00:17:23.879 --> 00:17:25.485
But it's really about seeing the world

00:17:25.485 --> 00:17:27.336
as it is right now accurately.

00:17:27.336 --> 00:17:28.188
Not worse than it is,

00:17:28.188 --> 00:17:29.490
but seeing the world accurately.

00:17:29.490 --> 00:17:32.424
Then seeing the world better than it is,

00:17:32.424 --> 00:17:34.367
and then developing a
strategy to get there.

00:17:34.367 --> 00:17:36.385
And one of the cornerstones
strategies for that

00:17:36.385 --> 00:17:38.147
is being able to persuade.

00:17:38.147 --> 00:17:40.537
To influence, to make your thoughts known

00:17:40.537 --> 00:17:41.853
in a way that empowers people

00:17:41.853 --> 00:17:44.004
and gets you want you want too.

